Description:
  The Switch Company result region: one page of companies a platform administrator may choose to
  administer.

  Rendered inline inside the Switch Company modal on first paint and swapped into that same region
  by htmx on search and paging, so the two are the same markup and cannot drift apart. Because the
  first page is server-rendered, the picker still works with no JavaScript at all: the search form
  is an ordinary GET and each pagination link is an ordinary link.

  Selecting is a POST carrying a CSRF token, never a link. Which company is being administered is
  an authorisation boundary rather than a display preference, so it can only be changed by a form
  submission the server can verify.

  The universe badge is shown because a platform administrator choosing between a real company and
  a generated one must be able to see which is which before choosing, not afterwards. The company
  chosen is what sets the workspace universe.

